# D1: the first attach with the four-card quad ON, on the AUDITED profile (c2-packed-tp4-gate-quad: every audit the gate profile
# carries, QWEN_FAST_QUAD_DRAFT=1 and QWEN_FAST_DRAFT_SINGLES_AUDIT=all). An all-four reset, then a smoke of a warmup, one coding
# stream, the mixed four-stream test (concurrent4: two prompts in the ramp, two steady: the quad refuses on 'ramp' and the pairs
# refuse too, every user drafts singly - the control for what the flag does to a mix it cannot serve) and the STEADY four-stream test
# (concurrent4_steady: four prompts of about 3,500 tokens, 800 tokens out: every user past the 2,048-row draft window from its first
# round, so the quad forms). This is the cheap run that puts the quad's 64-row pass on a card at four-card shapes for the first
# time (the card-M probe at four-card shapes is the one-card half): the matmul programs at per_core_M = 2, the SDPA at 32 query / 8
# KV heads over 2,080 keys, the 110-worker conv on four chips, the 62,080-column head as 2 chunks, and the four-user K/V copy. Every
# batched round is audited against the users' own single-user drafts. NOT a timed arm.
# A committed TEMPLATE of .github/c2-serving-job.env for the four-card batched-draft window (scripts/ci/c2_serving_job.py parses it):
# copy it over .github/c2-serving-job.env on a throwaway commit of tp4/draft and push a tag experiment/c2-serving-vN. Nothing here
# names a rig, a card or a registry: the cards are resolved at run time.
# ONE IMAGE FOR THE WHOLE WINDOW: C2_IMAGE_TAG names the image D0 builds from this same commit; a later commit needs a new tag.
# Duration (estimate): reset 1-3 min; the first engine build 10-30 min (kernel compile on a cold cache; the quad adds its SDPA,
# matmul and slice shapes, compiled inside the first quad round, 0.1-2 s once); the four tests 10-15 min: 20 / 40 / 90 min (a
# collective hang runs the 80-min ready loop, then the reset).
# Read: the ready line; the launched-argv line (profile c2-packed-tp4-gate-quad, QWEN_FAST_TP=4, QWEN_FAST_QUAD_DRAFT=1,
# QWEN_FAST_DRAFT_SINGLES_AUDIT=all); no attach refusal; in concurrent4_steady exactly ONE '[PINDIAG] quad draft engaged
# slots=[0,1,2,3] heads=32/8 rows=64 sdpa=fold conv=110', '[QUAD-DRAFT] round=N built=B ms=X' per quad round (the first built=1),
# '[PACKED-SELECT] round=N pairs=[[0, 1, 2, 3]] users=4' (the quad served it) and one '[DRAFT-SINGLES-AUDIT] round=N
# group=[0, 1, 2, 3] equal=1 stage=all checks=96' per audited round, every one equal=1; no '[QUAD-DRAFT] fallback' and no
# '[PINDIAG] quad draft disabled'; in concurrent4 the singles reasons ('[PACKED-PROPOSE] singles ... reasons=[ramp ...]') and no
# quad line; coherent text in coding and both four-stream tests; the verify t1 audit lines with no audit mismatch; the
# [PACKED-PHASE] and [PACKED-PUBLISH] lines.
# STOP on an attach refusal, a hang, an audit mismatch (verify or draft), garbage text, the quad never engaged or engaged twice, a
# quad fallback or disable line, or a ramp commit above 50 ms: the smoke step ENFORCES all of them (scripts/ci/c2_smoke_check.py exits
# non-zero), so the chain stops by itself. An unequal [DRAFT-SINGLES-AUDIT] line names the stage of the first difference
# (raw:values|indices:chunkN:chipC:uU, raw:projected:chipC:uU, features, candidates, scores, tokens): read it before anything else.
C2_CARDS=quad
C2_ACTIONS=reset smoke
C2_IMAGE_TAG=tp4-draft-1
C2_PROFILE=c2-packed-tp4-gate-quad
C2_SMOKE_TESTS=warmup,coding,concurrent4,concurrent4_steady
